      "card_ids": ["C27"],
      "claim": "Oxiracetam, a small polar molecule with high TPSA, showed absolute oral bioavailability of 59–92% in normal subjects, supporting that high polarity does not preclude F≥20%.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C24"],
      "claim": "Topiramate, a polar rigid monosaccharide-derived drug, is rapidly and well absorbed with oral bioavailability >80% in healthy volunteers, supporting high F for a highly functionalized rigid molecule.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "Doxifluridine, a polar nucleoside analog, achieved 80% oral bioavailability in patients, supporting high F despite extensive H-bonding capacity.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C30"],
      "claim": "Vorapaxar, a rigid polycyclic molecule, showed ~100% oral bioavailability in humans, demonstrating that rigid complex scaffolds can be completely absorbed.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C23"],
      "claim": "Tacrolimus, a complex macrocyclic natural product with poor solubility, still achieved mean oral bioavailability of 24% in transplant patients, directly supporting F≥20% for a complex rigid molecule.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "Cedazuridine, a polar nucleoside analog, had oral bioavailability of 20% in patients, meeting the F≥20% threshold and supporting high.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C28"],
      "claim": "Amphotericin B has negligible oral bioavailability due to poor permeability, low solubility, and gastric instability; this is the main contradictory evidence, but its extreme size and instability are not shared by the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The preponderance of highly transferable experimental evidence indicates oral bioavailability ≥20%; multiple polar, rigid, and complex molecules achieve high F, and the only low example (amphotericin B) is an extreme outlier. Therefore predict high.",
